\begin{cases} a + b = 6, \\ 4a + b = 12. \end{cases}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get $3a = 6,$ so $a = 2.$ Substituting $a = 2$ into the first equation, we get $2 + b = 6,$ so $b = 4.$ Therefore, the ordered pair $(a, b)$ is $(2, 4).$ </think> <answer> (2, 4) </answer>

